@startuml
' UC17.2 - Thêm học liệu Reading
autonumber "<b>0.</b> "
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor white
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor white
skinparam BoundaryBackgroundColor white
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor white
skinparam LifeLineBackgroundColor white
skinparam LifeLineBorderColor black
skinparam ArrowColor black
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor black
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam MaxMessageSize 200

' AS-IS evidence; paths are relative to the workspace root.
' UC/BR sources: docs/uml/docs/LearnUP_UseCase.docx (UC17.2) and
' docs/uml/docs/LearnUP_QuyTacNghiepVu.docx (BR-293, BR-286, BR-51, BR-151, BR-288, BR-285).
' Both documents have core revision 1, without an identified business release.
' Requested docs/ documents are under docs/uml/docs/; docs/source-of-truth is absent.
' UI: frontend/src/pages/instructor/course.builder.material.reading.add.tsx:29;
' handleFile :62, handleSave :93, warning handling :141, failure reload :175.
' Route: frontend/src/router.tsx:457, :459 and :501 (Instructor-protected Builder child).
' Wrappers: frontend/src/services/course.service.ts:177 and :187.
' Axios: frontend/src/services/axios.customize.ts:47, :61 and :64;
' URL selection: frontend/src/config/env.ts:13; frontend/.env.development:10 = localhost:8080.
' No frontend .env/.env.local/.env.development.local or process URL overrides were found.
' Gateway: gateway/api-gateway/src/main/resources/application.yml:2 and :40 (predicate :43).
' Course prefix/version: services/course-service/src/main.ts:40.
' Controller: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/courses.controller.ts:223 and :237.
' Service: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/courses.service.ts:1340 and :1411.
' Extraction: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/reading-text-extractor.ts:8 and :20.
' Repository: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/courses.repository.ts:882, :922, :1114, :1127.
' DTO: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/dto/create-reading-material.dto.ts:10.
' Multipart cap: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/course-values.ts:37 (50 MiB).
' Tenant adapter: services/course-service/src/infrastructure/clients/tenant/tenant.client.ts:64.
' Adapter timeout: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/courses.module.ts:14 (5000 ms).
' Tenant URL: services/course-service/.env:4 = http://localhost:8084.
' Tenant controller: services/tenant-service/src/modules/subscriptions/subscriptions.controller.ts:22;
' service: services/tenant-service/src/modules/subscriptions/subscriptions.service.ts:128;
' repository: services/tenant-service/src/modules/subscriptions/subscriptions.repository.ts:20.
' Tenant prefix/version: services/tenant-service/src/main.ts:34.
' Storage wiring: services/course-service/src/infrastructure/storage/storage.module.ts:7;
' selection: services/course-service/src/infrastructure/storage/storage.provider.ts:31.
' Three Cloudinary configuration values are present locally; values are not disclosed.
' Provider: libraries/ts-storage/src/providers/cloudinary/cloudinary.provider.ts:31 (upload),
' :61 (delete), :102 (uploadBuffer); raw resources use upload_stream, not Video chunk upload.
' Course models: services/course-service/prisma/schema.prisma:10, :104, :126 and :187.
' Tenant model: services/tenant-service/prisma/schema.prisma:133 (Subscription).
' Each PrismaService uses its own DATABASE_URL; local database names were verified.
' Running servers, live PlatformSetting rows and remote Cloudinary access are unverified.

actor Instructor
boundary "Add Reading Material Page" as Screen
participant ":ApiGateway" as Gateway
participant ":CoursesController" as Controller
participant ":CoursesService" as Service
participant ":CoursesRepository" as Repository
participant ":SubscriptionsController" as SubscriptionsController
participant ":SubscriptionsService" as SubscriptionsService
participant ":SubscriptionsRepository" as SubscriptionsRepository
participant ":CloudinaryStorageProvider" as Storage
participant "Cloudinary" as Cloudinary
database "course_db" as CourseDB
database "tenant_db" as TenantDB

' Preconditions: authenticated Instructor; Course Builder shell already loaded.
' Shared structure and Assessment outline preparation do not supply this upload operation.
' JWT middleware/token refresh are omitted. TenantClient is a hidden adapter:
' direct REST uses the internal key and trusted userId/organizationId/INSTRUCTOR headers.
activate Instructor
Instructor -> Screen: Open Add Reading Material
activate Screen
Screen -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/lessons/{lessonId}/materials/reading-upload-context
activate Gateway
Gateway -> Controller: GET /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/lessons/{lessonId}/materials/reading-upload-context
activate Controller
Controller -> Service: getReadingUploadContext(user, courseId, lessonId)
activate Service

' Outcome-level context trace expands only successful reads.
alt Upload context loaded successfully
  ' Require INSTRUCTOR and organizationId before the scoped read.
  Service -> Repository: findLessonForMaterialUpload\nCurrent organization and instructor
  activate Repository
  Repository -> CourseDB: Read assigned Lesson and Course state
  activate CourseDB
  CourseDB -->> Repository: Scoped Lesson and Course
  deactivate CourseDB
  Repository -->> Service: Scoped Lesson and Course
  deactivate Repository

  par Read Reading settings
    Service -> Repository: getReadingSettings()
    activate Repository
    Repository -> CourseDB: Read latest local PlatformSetting
    activate CourseDB
    CourseDB -->> Repository: PDF size limit, MIME types and reading speed
    deactivate CourseDB
    Repository -->> Service: Reading settings
    deactivate Repository
  and Read Subscription policy
    Service -> SubscriptionsController: GET /api/v1/subscriptions/internal/instructor-material-upload-policy
    activate SubscriptionsController
    SubscriptionsController -> SubscriptionsService: getInstructorMaterialUploadPolicy(user)
    activate SubscriptionsService
    SubscriptionsService -> SubscriptionsRepository: findCurrent(organizationId)
    activate SubscriptionsRepository
    SubscriptionsRepository -> TenantDB: Read current organization Subscription
    activate TenantDB
    TenantDB -->> SubscriptionsRepository: Subscription or none
    deactivate TenantDB
    SubscriptionsRepository -->> SubscriptionsService: Subscription or none
    deactivate SubscriptionsRepository
    ' Only an Active Subscription with startsAt <= now < expiresAt permits upload.
    SubscriptionsService -->> SubscriptionsController: Permission and storage limit
    deactivate SubscriptionsService
    SubscriptionsController -->> Service: 200 OK - upload policy
    deactivate SubscriptionsController
  and Read organization usage
    Service -> Repository: getOrganizationStoredBytes(organizationId)
    activate Repository
    Repository -> CourseDB: Sum Ready, unreleased MediaFile bytes
    activate CourseDB
    CourseDB -->> Repository: Used bytes
    deactivate CourseDB
    Repository -->> Service: Used bytes
    deactivate Repository
  end
  Service -->> Controller: Eligibility, PDF limits and remaining storage
  deactivate Service
  Controller -->> Gateway: 200 OK - Reading upload context
  deactivate Controller
  Gateway -->> Screen: Reading upload context
  deactivate Gateway

  alt Upload eligibility checked successfully\nUpload allowed
    Screen -->> Instructor: Show PDF form and limits\nLocked Course permits Optional only
    Instructor -> Screen: Choose PDF, title and requirement
    Screen -> Screen: Validate selected file and fields
    activate Screen
    deactivate Screen

    alt Form validated successfully
      Instructor -> Screen: Click Upload Reading
      ' Browser FormData contains title, string isRequired and binary file, no wordCount.
      ' Locked context forces isRequired=false. Axios upload timeout=120000 ms.
      Screen -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/lessons/{lessonId}/materials/readings\nMultipart: title, isRequired, file
      activate Gateway
      Gateway -> Controller: POST /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/lessons/{lessonId}/materials/readings\nMultipart file and trusted user context
      activate Controller
      ' Memory FileInterceptor: one file, two fields, three parts, max 50 MiB.
      ' Multipart/DTO failures can stop before Service; framework short-circuits are omitted.
      Controller -> Service: uploadReadingMaterial(user, courseId, lessonId, dto, file)
      activate Service

      ' Outcome-level creation trace; failures do not imply successful remote work or writes.
      alt Reading created successfully
        Service -> Repository: Recheck assigned Lesson and load Reading settings
        activate Repository
        ' Sequential source methods: findLessonForMaterialUpload then getReadingSettings.
        Repository -> CourseDB: Read current Lesson state and Reading limits
        activate CourseDB
        CourseDB -->> Repository: Scoped Lesson and settings
        deactivate CourseDB
        Repository -->> Service: Scoped Lesson and settings
        deactivate Repository
        Service -> Service: Validate Course state, PDF signature and size
        activate Service
        ' Early allow-list: Draft/Rejected/Published, neither Course nor Lesson disabled.
        ' Locked+isRequired=true is rejected. PDF MIME must also be allowed in settings.
        ' Positive safe-integer size <= min(settings.maxReadingSizeBytes, 50 MiB);
        ' buffer length >=8 and first five ASCII bytes must equal %PDF-.
        deactivate Service
        Service -> SubscriptionsController: GET /api/v1/subscriptions/internal/instructor-material-upload-policy
        activate SubscriptionsController
        SubscriptionsController -> SubscriptionsService: getInstructorMaterialUploadPolicy(user)
        activate SubscriptionsService
        SubscriptionsService -> SubscriptionsRepository: findCurrent(organizationId)
        activate SubscriptionsRepository
        SubscriptionsRepository -> TenantDB: Read current organization Subscription
        activate TenantDB
        TenantDB -->> SubscriptionsRepository: Subscription or none
        deactivate TenantDB
        SubscriptionsRepository -->> SubscriptionsService: Subscription or none
        deactivate SubscriptionsRepository
        ' Only an Active Subscription with startsAt <= now < expiresAt permits upload.
        SubscriptionsService -->> SubscriptionsController: Permission and storage limit
        deactivate SubscriptionsService
        SubscriptionsController -->> Service: 200 OK - upload policy
        deactivate SubscriptionsController
        Service -> Repository: Check organization storage usage
        activate Repository
        Repository -> CourseDB: Sum Ready, unreleased MediaFile bytes
        activate CourseDB
        CourseDB -->> Repository: Used bytes
        deactivate CourseDB
        Repository -->> Service: Used bytes
        deactivate Repository

        Service -> Service: Extract PDF text and count words
        activate Service
        ' Actual local function: extractReadingText(file.buffer), using pdf-parse max:0.
        ' countWords normalizes NFC/NBSP and counts whitespace tokens containing a letter/number.
        ' Successful parsing with zero words returns wordCount=0 and extractionWarning.
        ' Parse exceptions become 400 BEFORE any storage upload, not zero-word success.
        ' No OCR, remote document service or separate extractor class is called.
        deactivate Service

        Service -> Storage: Upload PDF buffer as raw resource
        activate Storage
        Storage -> Cloudinary: Upload Reading PDF
        activate Cloudinary
        Cloudinary -->> Storage: Stored-file metadata
        deactivate Cloudinary
        Storage -->> Service: Stored file and actual size
        deactivate Storage
        ' Service requires returned size >0 and <= effective Reading limit.
        ' A fresh policy is requested after storage, before database persistence.
        Service -> SubscriptionsController: GET /api/v1/subscriptions/internal/instructor-material-upload-policy
        activate SubscriptionsController
        SubscriptionsController -> SubscriptionsService: getInstructorMaterialUploadPolicy(user)
        activate SubscriptionsService
        SubscriptionsService -> SubscriptionsRepository: findCurrent(organizationId)
        activate SubscriptionsRepository
        SubscriptionsRepository -> TenantDB: Read current organization Subscription
        activate TenantDB
        TenantDB -->> SubscriptionsRepository: Subscription or none
        deactivate TenantDB
        SubscriptionsRepository -->> SubscriptionsService: Subscription or none
        deactivate SubscriptionsRepository
        ' Only an Active Subscription with startsAt <= now < expiresAt permits upload.
        SubscriptionsService -->> SubscriptionsController: Permission and storage limit
        deactivate SubscriptionsService
        SubscriptionsController -->> Service: 200 OK - upload policy
        deactivate SubscriptionsController
        Service -> Repository: createReadingMaterialWithQuota(...)
        activate Repository
        Repository -> CourseDB: Recheck quota and Course under locks\nSave wordCount and append Reading material
        activate CourseDB
        ' One transaction, timeout=20 s: upsert/lock organization_quota_locks, lock Course,
        ' recheck tenant/chain owner/status/disabled/Locked-required and aggregate usage.
        ' Insert MediaFile(purpose=LessonReading, status=Ready, storage metadata, wordCount),
        ' then Material(materialType=Reading, isRequired, fileId, position=max+1).
        ' Zero words do not block creation. Extracted text/warning are not stored here.
        CourseDB -->> Repository: Committed Reading material
        deactivate CourseDB
        Repository -->> Service: CREATED and material
        deactivate Repository
        Service -->> Controller: Material, size, wordCount and extractionWarning
        deactivate Service
        Controller -->> Gateway: 201 Created - Reading material
        deactivate Controller
        Gateway -->> Screen: Created material and extraction result
        deactivate Gateway

        alt Reading saved successfully\nText extracted
          Screen -->> Instructor: Show saved word count and open material list
        else Reading saved successfully\nNo readable text
          ' The parser succeeded; an image-only scan can produce this result.
          ' Persisted wordCount=0; extractionWarning describes missing reading duration.
          Screen -->> Instructor: Show saved-with-zero-words warning\nStay on page and clear selected file
        end
      else Reading creation failed
        activate Gateway
        activate Controller
        activate Service
        ' 400: invalid title/file/MIME/PDF signature, parse exception or returned size.
        ' 413: input size cap; 403: wrong role/missing organization or disallowed policy.
        ' 404: inaccessible Lesson/Course/tenant/chain owner.
        ' 409: Submitted or other disallowed state, disabled, Locked-required or insufficient quota.
        ' Tenant non-2xx/malformed policy/transport failure/5000 ms timeout ->503.
        ' No retry or permissive fallback; no downstream reply/completion after timeout assumed.
        ' StorageProviderError ->503, storage validation ->400, unexpected DB error ->500.
        opt Stored file returned and transaction not committed
          Service -> Storage: Delete uncommitted uploaded file
          activate Storage
          Storage -> Cloudinary: Delete stored resource
          activate Cloudinary
          Cloudinary -->> Storage: Deletion result or error
          deactivate Cloudinary
          Storage -->> Service: Cleanup result or error
          deactivate Storage
          ' Finally awaits best-effort cleanup; cleanup failure is logged, original error retained.
        end
        Service -->> Controller: Validation, policy, storage or persistence error
        deactivate Service
        Controller -->> Gateway: 400 / 403 / 404 / 409 / 413 / 503 or 500
        deactivate Controller
        Gateway -->> Screen: Reading creation error
        deactivate Gateway
        Screen -->> Instructor: Show upload error
      end

      opt Upload failed or extraction warning returned
        ' Both UI branches call query.reload(). Normal success navigates away instead.
        Screen -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/lessons/{lessonId}/materials/reading-upload-context
        activate Gateway
        Gateway -> Controller: GET /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/lessons/{lessonId}/materials/reading-upload-context
        activate Controller
        Controller -> Service: Reload Reading upload context
        activate Service
        ' Same getReadingUploadContext internals as above, including Tenant REST and
        ' parallel settings/usage reads; repeated internals are not expanded.
        Service -->> Controller: Refreshed context or load error
        deactivate Service
        Controller -->> Gateway: 200 OK or context error
        deactivate Controller
        Gateway -->> Screen: Context result
        deactivate Gateway
        Screen -->> Instructor: Show refreshed form, warning, block or load error
        ' Warning survives reload, disables further input/upload, and offers View saved Reading.
        ' While reloading, the page displays Skeleton; a reload failure shows the load error.
      end
    else Form validation failed
      ' No POST for missing/invalid title, file, MIME, size or insufficient remaining storage.
      Screen -->> Instructor: Show validation error
    end
  else Upload eligibility failed
    ' GET returns 200 with canUpload=false for disallowed Course/disabled Lesson,
    ' or a Subscription outside its Active validity period. Locked alone is allowed.
    Screen -->> Instructor: Show block reason and disable upload
  end
else Upload context loading failed
  activate Gateway
  activate Controller
  activate Service
  ' Role/organization ->403, inaccessible Lesson ->404, absent settings/Tenant failure ->503.
  ' Failed context preparation assumes no successful queries and emits no multipart POST.
  Service -->> Controller: Context access or verification error
  deactivate Service
  Controller -->> Gateway: 403 / 404 / 503 or server error
  deactivate Controller
  Gateway -->> Screen: Context load error
  deactivate Gateway
  Screen -->> Instructor: Show load error and Try again
end
deactivate Screen
deactivate Instructor

' BR-293: a valid parsed PDF with no counted words is stored with wordCount=0 and a warning;
' a PDF parse exception (for example, a corrupted or password-protected file)
' becomes an error and stops upload; the parser determines which PDFs it can read.
' BR-286/285: Locked accepts only Optional and every new material is appended;
' early checks allow only Draft/Rejected/Published, rejecting Submitted/Archived/disabled.
' Final transaction explicitly rejects Submitted, Archived, Disabled and disabledAt,
' then Locked-required. Its named status exclusions are narrower than the early allow-list.
' Ownership follows Lesson/Module/Course organizationId and Course.chain.instructorId.
' BR-151: validate configured PDF MIME/size and Subscription quota, then recheck before commit.
' BR-288: usage sums Ready, unreleased MediaFile rows once, not Material/version references.
' There is no explicit purpose whitelist in the aggregate; the quota lock serializes
' cooperating writers, not arbitrary writes or Subscription changes in tenant_db.
' Latest policy and Course DB commit do not form one cross-database transaction.
' BR-51 evidence only, outside this upload interaction:
' CoursesRepository.calculateEstimatedDurationMinutes at courses.repository.ts:329
' uses CEIL(file.wordCount/currentReadingSpeed) for Required, non-disabled Readings.
' Optional Readings are excluded; zero words contribute zero minutes. Upload persists
' wordCount/isRequired only; it does not execute that query, open UC14.1 or publish an event.
' No handwritten word count input, OCR, MinIO, presigned URL or direct browser storage upload.
' UI progress=100% confirms browser transfer only. POST timeout=120 s does not prove
' backend cancellation, cleanup or rollback; remote credential validity remains unverified.
' If provider upload throws before returning a storage key, service cleanup cannot target
' that remote resource; cleanup failures are only logged, without retry.
' Error caveat: Axios resolves HTTP error bodies; missing response.data.id throws a plain
' Error. toApiError can then map it to status 0, bypassing intended status-specific messages.
' Warning/failed POST reloads are shown; ordinary UC17 list loading after navigation is omitted.
' No LearningClient, Kafka, notification, audit, Video upload, replacement or user deletion.
@enduml
